Recorded request/response pairs of rmig apply/verify/rollback against a local indexer,
2026-11-17: wazuh-indexer 5.0.0-rc1 (content manager 5.0.0, OpenSearch 3.6.0). Input: tests/data/api/out-live
(one rules-only integration, no decoders, so no root_decoder is left on the indexer) and
tests/data/api/alerts-live.json.

Each file: {"command", "exit", "calls": [{"method", "path", "request", "status", "response"}]}.
Recorded inside rmig.api.client.Client.call: no headers, no credentials. The indexer was shared: _search
responses also hold documents of another user. Their author and description text was replaced by neutral
values ("other-user", "Content of another user."); the response shapes are as returned.

Sequence and what each one shows:
  01 apply --dry-run      reads only; prints the writes
  02 apply                POST integration, POST rule, GET/POST /promote draft -> test (ids + policy)
  03 apply                idempotent: no write
  04 verify               400 "Integration [...] not found in the 'test' space": between 03 and 04
                          another user reset and promoted the draft, which removed the tool's content
                          from draft and test
  05 apply                recreated after that external reset
  06 verify               on-stock path: /logtest/normalization (standard) + /logtest/detection
                          (test): REPRODUCED
  07, 08 rollback         DELETE of the integration answers 500 "Log Type ... cannot be deleted
                          because active rules exist" while test still has its rule: rollback is
                          two-phase (content, promote, integrations, promote)
  09, 10 rollback         stopped before any write: the draft had pending changes of another user,
                          listed; the external reset had already removed the tool's content (search by
                          the mark: 0 documents)
